\description{
\strong{Experimental.} Build a \link[crew:crew_controller]{crew::crew_controller} whose workers run on
remote machines over SSH, for distributing a \code{targets} pipeline (or any
\code{crew} workload) across several computers on a trusted local network. Workers
are placed across nodes in proportion to per-node capacities (\code{caps}), so
heterogeneous machines can share a single controller. See \code{\link[=crew_ssh_node]{crew_ssh_node()}}
for per-node overrides and \link{crew_class_launcher_ssh} for the placement rule.
}
\section{Requirements}{

Each worker is launched with \verb{ssh <host> "cd <projdir> && <rscript> -e '<crew_worker call>'"} and must be able to dial back into the controller over
the network. In practice this needs:
\itemize{
\item passwordless SSH (keys) from the control machine to every node;
\item the same project + R library reachable at \code{projdir} on every node (for
example a shared network filesystem, or identical local checkouts);
\item for direct dial-back (\code{tunnel = FALSE}): \code{host} set to an address the worker
nodes can reach (NOT \verb{127.0.0.1}) with the dispatcher's TCP port reachable;
\item for \code{tunnel = TRUE}: nothing extra -- the dial-back rides the SSH connection,
so no inbound port is opened (best for firewalled networks).
}
